# Raw datasets must be stored byte-for-byte.
#
# The AI4I CSV ships with CRLF line endings. Without `-text` git applies its
# text/EOL heuristics, which rewrote the blob to LF on the first commit and
# left the repository holding a file whose SHA-256 did not match the checksum
# recorded in data/README.md. `-text` disables all conversion in both
# directions, so a clone always reproduces the documented bytes.
data/raw/*.csv -text

# Lockfiles must not be rewritten either.
package-lock.json -text
